<title>USA: Compaq Computer Corp Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Compaq Computer Corp Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENT OF INCOME</p>
<p>			    (Unaudited)</p>
<p>			     Year ended		 Quarter ended</p>
<p>			     December 31,		December 31,</p>
<p>				1996	  1995     1996	 1995</p>
<p>			    (in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p> Sales		  $ 18,109    $ 14,755  $ 5,422    $ 4,701</p>
<p>Research and</p>
<p>  development costs	407	   270	105	   81</p>
<p>Purchased in-process  </p>
<p>  technology (1)			   241		     241</p>
<p>			     2,320	 2,200	662	  812</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>provision for income</p>
<p>   taxes		   1,876	 1,188	661	  207</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>  income taxes	     563	   399	199	  125</p>
<p> Net income		1,313	   789	462	   82</p>
<p>Earnings per common</p>
<p>and common equivalent share:</p>
<p>   Primary		  4.72	  2.88     1.64	 0.30</p>
<p>Assuming full</p>
<p>    dilution		4.66	  2.87     1.64	 0.30</p>
<p>Shares used in</p>
<p>computing earnings per common</p>
<p>and common equivalent share:</p>
<p>     Primary	     278.3	 273.6    282.1	276.0</p>
<p>Assuming full</p>
<p>	dilution	   281.4	 275.0    282.1	276.0</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) Represents a $241 million ($0.87 per share) non-recurring, non-tax deductible charge for purchased in-process technology in connection with the NetWorth and Thomas-Conrad acquisitions during the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>Prior to the charge, 1995 Q4 earnings were $1.17 per share.</p>
<p>First Call consensus for 1996 Q4 was $1.53 per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
